  "notes": "Five kicks to the bar and everything else follows them: 1, the a of 1, the and of 2, then 3 and the a of 3 — a 3-3-2 lurch that nothing else in the roster plays, with a sixth kick thrown in about a quarter of the time. The backbeat stays full-time on 2 and 4 with a clap layered on it, the bed-squeak and vocal-chop percs land anywhere on the 16ths at a density that makes them part of the beat rather than a garnish, and the melody is a bright sample flip that goes major as often as minor. At 138 the kick pattern is the hook.",
